      "servedBy": "meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026",
      "text": "**Built in configurator:** 2-storey Hex Cluster column (0,0,0 + 0,0,1 full) with adjacent cut-face columns (1,0,0 + 1,0,1 half-n) joined with joint bolts, providing two drawer-ready bases and two tiered surfaces approximating shelf levels. Mesh verified `clear`.\n\n**Critical limitation:** This configurator verifies **fit / geometry and mesh clearance only - it does NOT verify mechanical strength, load rating, shelving capacity, or weight limits.** The instruction explicitly prohibits claiming load ratings. No Hex Cluster part in the catalog is listed as \"shelf rated to X kg\", and `check_build` does not check load.\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence / Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shelf unit rated to hold 50 kg of books | **unmet** | No load-rating is modeled or enforced by `get_build`/`check_build`/`find_parts`. The build provides two tiered hex bases (piece:0,0,0;full + piece:0,0,1;full with snap) that can be used as shelf-like platforms/brackets can be added (hex-acc-bracket exists), but **I cannot claim or verify 50 kg capacity**. A rated shelf would require external structural engineering outside this tool. Built as a modest 2-level demonstrator instead. |\n| Two drawers | **met** | drawer:0#1,0#cut on piece:1,0,0;half-n and drawer:1#1,0#cut on piece:1,0,1;half-n — both placed via configurator drawer sockets s22/s23 and verified. |\n\n**Summary:** Physical arrangement for a 2-drawer shelf unit created and mesh-clear, but the *50 kg rating* cannot be met or verified within Hex Cluster configurator, which is geometry-only per rules — therefore marked unmet.\n",
